utting of fuel lines that spanned the structure.This caused an intense in-flight fire in the engine bay.","factors":[{"id":"cfit","role":"outcome","evidence":"Cfit."},{"id":"loss_of_control_inflight","role":"outcome","evidence":"Loss Of Control Inflight."},{"id":"engine_failure","role":"initiating","evidence":"Engine Failure."},{"id":"inflight_fire","role":"outcome","evidence":"Inflight Fire."},{"id":"metal_fatigue","role":"contributing","evidence":"Metal Fatigue."},{"id":"uncontained_engine_failure","role":"initiating","evidence":"Uncontained Engine Failure."},{"id":"fatigue","role":"contributing","evidence":"Fatigue."},{"id":"terrorism_or_hostile_act","role":"initiating","evidence":"Terrorism Or Hostile Act."},{"id":"emergency_landing","role":"outcome","evidence":"Emergency Landing."}],"chain":[["engine_failure","loss_of_control_inflight"]],"events":[{"t":0,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"CAPT","kind":"system","text":"Takeoff occurred","factors":[]},{"t":600,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":"crew_action","text":"Landing occurred","factors":[]},{"t":1200,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":"crew_action","text":"Crashed occurred","factors":[]},{"t":1800,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":"crew_action","text":"Engine failure occurred","factors":[]},{"t":9999,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":"outcome","text":"Aircraft crashed","factors":[]}],"report_links":["https://aviation-safety.net/database/record.php?id=19761012-0","https://archive.today/20130124222408/http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=5gs1AAAAIBAJ&sjid=EU8KAAAAIBAJ&pg=5582,2496393&dq=indian+airlines+bombay+crash&hl=en","https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=z-8vAAAAIBAJ&sjid=gV0DAAAAIBAJ&pg=3759,3374820&dq=indian+airlines+bombay+crash&hl=en"],"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Airlines_Flight_171","asn_id":"19761012-0","interest":16.77,"extraction":{"method":"llm","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","confidence":"high","reviewed":false,"notes":[]}},{"id":"wd_q18466708","qid":"Q18466708","tier":"wikidata","depth":"summary","title":"1976 Lloyd Aéreo Boliviano Boeing 707 crash","flight_number":null,"date":"1976-10-13","agency":"NTSB","aircraft":{"type":"Boeing 707","manufacturer":"Boeing","family":"707","registration":"N 730JP"},"operator":"Lloyd Aereo Boliviano","route":{"from_name":"El Trompillo","to_name":"Florida"},"location":{"name":"El Trompillo Airport","country":"Bolivia"},"occupants":170,"fatalities":88,"phase":"takeoff","category":"UNK","summary":"On 13 October 1976, a Boeing 707, a chartered cargo aircraft operated for Lloyd Aéreo Boliviano (LAB) crashed shortly after takeoff at El Trompillo Airport, Santa Cruz de la Sierra, Bolivia, into a residential neighbourhood. All three crew on board were killed, along with 88 other fatalities on the ground, bringing the total up to 91. It is the deadliest air disaster to happen on Bolivian soil.","probable_cause":"The Flight Data Recorder was not serviceable at the time of the crash, and the Cockpit Voice Recorder did not obtain much information, as the cockpit microphone was inoperative.It was determined that improper flight preparation due to pilot fatigue was the main cause of the accident.","factors":[{"id":"cfit","role":"outcome","evidence":"Cfit."},{"id":"engine_failure","role":"initiating","evidence":"Engine Failure."},{"id":"inflight_fire","role":"outcome","evidence":"Inflight Fire."},{"id":"metal_fatigue","role":"contributing","evidence":"Metal Fatigue."},{"id":"fatigue","role":"contributing","evidence":"Fatigue."}],"chain":[],"events":[{"t":0,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"CAPT","kind":"system","text":"Takeoff occurred","factors":[]},{"t":600,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":"crew_action","text":"Crashed occurred","factors":[]},{"t":1200,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":"crew_action","text":"Fire occurred","factors":[]},{"t":9999,"clock":null,"phase":"takeoff","actor":"SYS","kind":